cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its frozen dataset, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "concurrent-cold: the value of cross-regional dependence of weather-forecast errors for US natural gas storage forecasts"
authors:
  - family-names: Mosca
    given-names: Antonio
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-4023-4664"
version: 0.1.0
url: "https://github.com/antoniomosca27/concurrent-cold"
repository-code: "https://github.com/antoniomosca27/concurrent-cold"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Real-time reconstruction of the information available on Friday evening and
  probabilistic forecasts of the weekly net withdrawal from US Lower-48 natural
  gas storage, comparing a calibrated national model with regional Monte Carlo
  models that sample NOAA forecast-error trajectories independently or jointly
  across the nine Census divisions.
keywords:
  - natural gas storage
  - probabilistic forecasting
  - weather forecast errors
  - spatial dependence
  - real-time data
  - Monte Carlo
  - C++
